// Title: an exhaustive struct alternative accepts a wider struct, so an
// or-pattern binds a field of another member's type.
// Command: graphix --no-cache c-pattern-or-struct-field-count.gx
//   (and --no-fusion; graphix-fuzz run on the same file)
// Expected: ["s!", "zz!"]: `{x, y}` names exactly the fields of
// {x: i64, y: string}, so the value {x: 1, y: 42, z: "zz"} takes the
// second alternative, whose y is field z. Or the check refuses the arm.
// Observed: the node-walk prints ["s!", "42!"] (y: string holds 42); with
// fusion the kernel panics: "kernel param `y`: runtime I64(42) does not
// match the compiled String slot" and the runtime dies.
// StructPatternNode::Struct's is_match tests `a.len() >= binds.len()` for
// an exhaustive pattern too, and footprint calls the two members apart.
type U = [{x: i64, y: string}, {x: i64, y: i64, z: string}];
let vs: Array<U> = [{x: 1, y: "s"}, {x: 1, y: 42, z: "zz"}];
array::map(vs, |v| select v {
  {x, y} | {x, y: _, z: y} => "[y]!"
})
